Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Bundles", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["[[ LLM Generated ]]",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"032b16a8-1040-405d-918a-4b0e92957eb1"],

Cell["\<\
We start with a finite graph and a projection of its vertices. Equal fibers, \
lift existence, unique lifting and bundle structure are separate properties. \
Sections and complete connections add choices to this data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9335253-e315-44bf-970c-ce9fe38255ee"],

Cell["Topological language and finite readings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"273de1ab-b9a1-484b-88f7-8311778bc1bf"],

Cell["\<\
The finite object is a graph with a vertex projection. The following \
dictionary distinguishes its exact conditions from the additional structures \
of continuous topology.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"458cd4b3-6b38-407e-b37e-f5943344ac2e"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "8b2e8647-9a9e-49a7-bb98-ff0252286e89"], Cell[
    "Topological notion", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"2d462263-943f-4889-b798-d0bd27bd573e"],
     Cell["Finite infra reading", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"6ac40be6-7ab8-42e2-ade3-b5763e3da90c"],
     Cell["Qualification", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"5d091c05-5ad7-4c59-9053-43b16550326b"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "03712769-ab57-4bd0-874a-d63682872871"], Cell[
    "Projection from total space to base", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "03040ec8-00cb-4b5c-a6a1-ad5f8b6d4316"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberedGraph with InfraTotalSpace, InfraBaseSpace and InfraProjection\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"79a8db3d-fd12-4421-9c00-099d6b4ca153"], 
    Cell["\<\
The base graph is reconstructed from projected edges; no topology is part of \
the inert object.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"dfbc01df-45c7-4453-90dc-2e7552ad2ae7"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "82ad3dbf-dac9-434c-9da2-ff373733290a"], Cell[
    "Serre or Hurewicz fibration", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7b07f3d9-c711-4f01-b091-7154c12d5c23"], Cell["\<\
InfraFibrationQ asks for a lift of every base edge from every starting vertex\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8fc09b61-b212-4e11-907b-50a2442a640b"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is weak edge-lift existence, not a homotopy-lifting axiom.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"3f1563da-f235-459d-bae8-0a5c0f9f322a"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "b412a7d2-6d3d-4a42-9579-41253d1cad5b"], Cell[
    "Covering space", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "b1426bc6-5e73-43fd-9898-7097a61b15f4"], Cell["\<\
InfraCoveringQ gives edgeless fibers and a bijection on vertex neighbourhoods\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8d78a600-7a00-40f7-a1af-364e8a7eb271"], 
    Cell["\<\
The graph-covering condition has the usual covering interpretation under \
graph realization. Sheet counts can differ across base components.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f9a108db-8042-49d0-9393-5ed793ff5e37"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "aeb03179-ede1-485d-8d62-4f1c20b0b009"], Cell[
    "Fiber bundle", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "d3b3a425-42b9-430a-aa39-186eb37c79bf"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberBundleQ gives a common fiber graph and adjacency-preserving \
transverse matchings\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b8033e22-ea4b-4280-8e5f-b43cf60b76aa"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is an edgewise Cartesian graph bundle. Realizing its edges alone does \
not supply topological product charts or filled squares.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f95c4f0a-cf9e-4fa1-bf74-bb202356409c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "ea61f2ff-e1d0-4980-8933-e871707513af"], Cell[
    "Section", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "9dd86443-1123-4ac0-9532-2288ad3cccf7"], Cell[
    "InfraSection chooses a right inverse on a base domain", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"8c633a3f-68c2-468f-9872-bcbd6e78f04c"], Cell["\<\
InfraContinuousSectionQ asks for adjacency preservation on that domain.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1bef3e55-b597-4563-8988-c1929f844459"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "e3659ba3-bcec-4cf5-be6b-2ca3e8bed8e1"], Cell[
    "Connection and parallel transport", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5422a7db-0430-4bcb-88f0-8a3372a6dfdc"], Cell["\<\
InfraConnection selects complete fiber matchings; transport composes them\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"82bc5f51-fd16-4aef-ba46-84b4b197efe7"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is finite bijective transport. Preserving a fiber graph is an additional \
condition.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"7e13887e-6f58-4b2b-a9d9-5cfba51b8e46"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4fbc6910-2026-46ef-b0a6-86834183affd"], Cell[
    "Infra-only transverse local conditions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e86e64d0-8325-471e-8313-19b43277e28a"], Cell["\<\
InfraAtMostOneEdgeLiftQ and InfraFibrationQ read injectivity and surjectivity \
on transverse neighbours\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8b3ae2e8-f00f-493d-af60-645dfa01e4ac"], 
    Cell["\<\
Vertical neighbours are excluded; the conditions do not assert local \
injectivity or surjectivity in a chosen topology.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"34e149d6-31b5-4d78-ac47-783f131e60b2"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "283f63ca-9763-4113-b38f-10cdbbd17c69"], Cell[
    "Infra-only multiplicity and equitable partition", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"19a4ce2a-456f-4b13-b147-d8c4ada35e8e"], Cell["\<\
InfraEdgeLiftMultiplicity counts transverse neighbours, including zeros\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0682581b-ab9b-45bf-8abe-8a2f0755b1c1"], 
    Cell["\<\
Constancy within each fiber is transverse equitability; full equitability \
also needs constant vertical degree.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"09b5d66a-92c5-47a2-997b-3641bb3c877f"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"1183767c-e9a5-43a8-974a-\
cb8ef7eb1023"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the continuous definitions, see ",
 ButtonBox["Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Sections 1.3 and 4.2",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf"], None}],
 ". The finite definitions and their implications are developed below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f52fe19d-1b79-4257-b1d5-86de24ce11a7"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"153f3b5c-1b59-4d84-bbe8-95c2ee216447"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", " ", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`\>\"", " ", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"de08d979-034c-479e-828c-f74daa6061f7"],

Cell["Total space, projection and fibers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"583198e2-19e5-491b-8923-805531604fe8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["fibered graph", "TI"],
 " consists of a finite simple undirected unweighted untagged graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eedf4087-f9b6-45a9-8592-52316463bc92"],
 " and a map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c36a8680-15f2-48b7-8650-2bb1c01c93eb"],
 " on its vertices. The ",
 StyleBox["base graph", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0be07330-8fdd-4c7f-a932-3aae94765953"],
 " has vertex set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec1fa470-8d7c-4be2-9571-80c06b1aeb70"],
 ". Distinct base vertices are adjacent exactly when some total edge joins \
their preimages. The ",
 StyleBox["fiber", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01c0956d-93d9-4af0-ac45-1f2b07726101"],
 " is the induced graph on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec255303-a485-419b-9a52-2b4a0fd91d9c"],
 ". A total edge is ",
 StyleBox["vertical", "TI"],
 " when both endpoints project to the same vertex, and ",
 StyleBox["transverse", "TI"],
 " otherwise."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4fb79ccb-9347-410e-ae95-e60d75f5da8c"],

Cell["\<\
The object carries no drawing, connection or lifting axiom. The base includes \
isolated projection values, and projection collapses vertical edges. The \
empty graph with empty projection is allowed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"acca4dc5-622c-4f19-994c-05be6651899f"],

